<!DOCTYPE suzuki [
<!ENTITY % sdatacharaents SYSTEM "..\config8\sdatacharaents.txt">
%sdatacharaents;
]>
<suzuki><manual>
<section sectnbr = "2D">
<servcat sctnbr = "02" scnbr = "04">
<configtype typenbr = "0">
<servinfotype sitcode = "6">
<servinfo servinfosgmlid = "AENLSB0A2406001" svcinfotypenbr = "08" svcinfoqualnbr = "01" page = "2" supplyoff = "1" modify = "0">
<title>
Wheel (with Tire) Removal and Installation
</title>
<servinfosub id = "AENLSB0A2406001001">
<title>
Removal
</title>
<attention4>
<ptxt>
Using heat to loosen a tight wheel nut for removal may shorten the life of the wheel and damage the wheel bearings.
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
Never use heat to loosen a wheel nut for removal.
</ptxt>
</attention4>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Loosen wheel nuts by approximately 180&#176;.
</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "IDAA0A240002.jpg" width = "88.000mm" height = "46.047mm" ver = "02" gw = "189" gh = "114"/>
</figure>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Hoist vehicle.
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Remove wheel with tire.
</ptxt>
</s1>
</servinfosub>
<servinfosub id = "AENLSB0A2406001002">
<title>
Installation
</title>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Before installing wheels, check the following points.
</ptxt>
<list1 type = "unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>
Check for buildup of corrosion / foreign material on mating surfaces of wheel (1) and brake disc / drum (2), and remove any buildup if any.
</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "IGAD0A240002.swf" width = "88.000mm" height = "71.992mm" ver = "01" gw = "169" gh = "188"/>
</figure>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>
Check for roughness, scoring or stepped wear on surfaces of nut taper (1) and wheel holes (2), and if any abnormality is found, repair or replace wheel nut and/or wheel.
</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "IGAD0A240003.swf" width = "88.000mm" height = "38.859mm" ver = "01" gw = "218" gh = "94"/>
</figure>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>
Check that any foreign material, rust, oil and grease are removed from thread part of wheel nut (1) and hub bolts (2).
</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "IGAD0A240004.swf" width = "88.000mm" height = "88.560mm" ver = "01" gw = "230" gh = "235"/>
</figure>
</item>
</list1>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Install each wheel nut by hand and if it is not screwed until nut comes in contact with seat of wheel hole or any abnormality is found, replace wheel nut and/or hub bolt.
</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "IGAD0A240005.swf" width = "88.000mm" height = "65.671mm" ver = "01" gw = "198" gh = "170"/>
</figure>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Lower vehicle and tighten wheel nuts in numerical order (“1” – “5”) to specified torque.
</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>
Tightening order
</title>
<ptxt>
“1” – “2” – “3” –“4” – “5”
</ptxt>
</spec>
<torque>
<torqueitem id = "T2D001">
<t-part>
Wheel nut*
</t-part>
<t-part1>
a
</t-part1>
<t-value1>
100
</t-value1>
<t-value2>
10.2
</t-value2>
<t-value3>
74.0
</t-value3>
</torqueitem>
</torque>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "IHSB0A240001.swf" width = "88.000mm" height = "60.045mm" ver = "01" gw = "163" gh = "154"/>
</figure>
</s1>
</servinfosub>
</servinfo>
</servinfotype>
</configtype>
</servcat>
</section></manual></suzuki>
